    "goal": "Size a GWAS genotype dataset's PLINK binary .bed storage: whole-dataset .bed size (MB), per-chromosome file count, and per-chromosome .bed size (MB) for the largest chromosome.",
    "rationale": "PLINK binary .bed packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte). Whole-dataset size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6. Per-chromosome size uses the same rule applied to one chromosome's variant count. The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of distinct chromosomes in the .bim; with 22 autosomes + X + Y (+ optional MT) the conventional split is 24-25 files, but the exact count must be read from the .bim chromosome IDs.",
